{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_4>\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    MOD = 1000000007\n    T = 1\n    \n    for _ in range(T):\n        P, K = map(int, input().split())\n        \n        if K == 0:\n            print(pow(P, P - 1, MOD))\n            continue\n        \n        # Create the mapping f(x) = K*x mod P\n        f = lambda x: (K * x) % P\n        \n        # Find cycles using DFS-like traversal\n        visited = [False] * P\n        cycle_lengths = []\n        \n        for start in range(P):\n            if visited[start]:\n                continue\n            \n            # Trace the orbit\n            current = start\n            length = 0\n            while not visited[current]:\n                visited[current] = True\n                current = f(current)\n                length += 1\n            \n            cycle_lengths.append(length)\n        \n        # Count occurrences of each cycle length\n        from collections import defaultdict\n        count_by_length = defaultdict(int)\n        for length in cycle_lengths:\n            count_by_length[length] += 1\n        \n        # Compute answer\n        ans = 1\n        for length, count in count_by_length.items():\n            effective = length * count + (1 if length > 1 else 0)\n            ans = (ans * pow(effective, count, MOD)) % MOD\n        \n        print(ans)\n\nmain()\n</your_rewritten_code_4>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007;\n    \n    static long pow(long base, long exp, long mod) {\n        long result = 1;\n        base %= mod;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                result = (result * base) % mod;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] line = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        int P = Integer.parseInt(line[0]);\n        int K = Integer.parseInt(line[1]);\n        \n        if (K == 0) {\n            System.out.println(pow(P, P - 1, MOD));\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        // Create the mapping f(x) = K*x mod P\n        int[] f = new int[P];\n        for (int i = 0; i < P; i++) {\n            f[i] = (K * i) % P;\n        }\n        \n        // Find cycles using DFS-like traversal\n        boolean[] visited = new boolean[P];\n        List<Integer> cycleLengths = new ArrayList<>();\n        \n        for (int start = 0; start < P; start++) {\n            if (visited[start]) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            \n            // Trace the orbit\n            int current = start;\n            int length = 0;\n            while (!visited[current]) {\n                visited[current] = true;\n                current = f[current];\n                length++;\n            }\n            cycleLengths.add(length);\n        }\n        \n        // Count occurrences of each cycle length\n        Map<Integer, Integer> countByLength = new HashMap<>();\n        for (int length : cycleLengths) {\n            countByLength.put(length, countByLength.getOrDefault(length, 0) + 1);\n        }\n        \n        // Compute answer\n        long ans = 1;\n        for (Map.Entry<Integer, Integer> entry : countByLength.entrySet()) {\n            int length = entry.getKey();\n            int count = entry.getValue();\n            int effective = length * count + (length > 1 ? 1 : 0);\n            ans = (ans * pow(effective, count, MOD)) % MOD;\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.536288416711614e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0001984637783607468, -1.2040065485052764e-05, -0.02980179339647293, -0.31342199444770813, -0.00042143522296100855, -2.539125671319198e-05, -0.027231140062212944, -0.0008189899963326752, -0.00038652101648040116, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -8.010543388081715e-05, -0.011050572618842125, -0.0010333680547773838, -0.025660216808319092, -0.0004586121649481356, -0.0009502424509264529, -5.483612312673358e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.08315201848745346, -8.940656698541716e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.6329566836357117, -4.5298504119273275e-05, -0.011578856967389584, -0.0013853248674422503, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.843663479434326e-05, -0.0008181562297977507, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.311301275563892e-06, -0.00018249277491122484, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -0.000676998752169311, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -